      "report_blocks": [
        {
          "text": "### Applicable Subscription Plans\nThe web interface at `gemini.google.com` (Gemini Apps) can be accessed under two distinct tiers of service:\n* **Consumer / Personal Plans:** Free Google accounts and **Gemini Advanced** (via Google One AI Premium).\n* **Business & Enterprise Plans:** **Google Workspace** editions with Gemini (including **Gemini Business**, **Gemini Enterprise**, and **Gemini for Education**) which grant enterprise-grade data protections and administrative governance.\n\n---\n\n### Governance Attributes\n\n#### 1. `sso_available`\n* **Consumer Plans:** Not available. Access relies on standard personal Google Account authentication.\n* **Enterprise / Google Workspace Plans:** **Yes.** When accessed with a work or school account, `gemini.google.com` inherits the Google Workspace organization's identity configuration, which supports Single Sign-On (SSO) via SAML 2.0 or OIDC third-party Identity Providers (IdPs), as well as Google as the IdP.\n\n#### 2. `data_retention`\n* **Consumer Plans:** Managed under **Gemini Apps Activity**. By default, conversations are retained for **18 months**, with user settings to set auto-deletion at 3 months, 36 months, or indefinite. If Gemini Apps Activity is turned off, conversations are temporarily retained for up to **72 hours** to provide the service and process feedback. Data selected for human review is decoupled from the Google account and kept for up to **3 years**.\n* **Enterprise / Google Workspace Plans:** Admins control conversation history policies. Conversation history is retained by default for **18 months**, and administrators can configure auto-deletion at 3, 18, or 36 months, or turn history off completely. Organizations can also govern retention, legal holds, and eDiscovery using **Google Vault**.\n\n#### 3. `training_on_customer_data`\n* **Consumer Plans:** **Yes.** Conversations, prompts, and related usage data may be human-reviewed and used by Google to train and improve machine learning models and Google products.\n* **Enterprise / Google Workspace Plans:** **No.** Under Google Workspace enterprise data protections, prompts, uploaded files, and generated responses stay within the organization and are **not** reviewed by humans or used to train Google's foundation AI models without explicit customer permission.\n\n#### 4. `admin_controls_available`\n* **Consumer Plans:** **No.** Controls are restricted to personal user-level settings.\n* **Enterprise / Google Workspace Plans:** **Yes.** Google Admin Console provides granular administrative controls, including:\n  * Turning the Gemini app on or off for specific organizational units (OUs) or groups.\n  * Managing organization-wide conversation history and retention settings.\n  * Restricting sharing of Gemini app conversations.\n  * Regulating data access permissions, Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies, and auditing activities through Google Vault and the Security Investigation Tool.\n\n#### 5. `enterprise_plan_available`\n* **Yes.** Enterprise plans are available via Google Workspace with **Gemini Business**, **Gemini Enterprise**, and Google Workspace for Education editions, enabling enterprise-level agreements, compliance coverage (e.g., HIPAA, FERPA), and enterprise data protection terms for `gemini.google.com`.",
